  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Achieving transformative results on the social norms and practices that perpetuate Gender based viol</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is in Belo and Batibo subdivisions, in the NorthWest Region of Cameroon. The project support the participation of women and girl members of women&#x2019;s and disability organizations in humanitarian decision making, does safety audits for women and girls and inform other clusters to implement risk mitigation measures._x000d_
-Provide cash assistance to 50 women and girls in the context of GBV case management (medical bills, transportation)._x000d_
-Build the capacity of social workers and community agents on GBV and available services_x000d_
-Strengthen data collection and information management_x000d_
-Build the capacity of community leaders and youth on the basic concepts of GBV, including gender equality and the survivor centered approach_x000d_
-Engage men and boys as allies in GBV prevention and community dialogues to publicly raise voices on gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
